! mcp_bootstrap_p128.strap -- the CHANNEL-SIGNAL / CONCEPTOR interrupt
! supervisor, printed page 128.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.135,
! header READ and not assumed: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
!  CARD ID EB000300   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  128", and
! the header's own "LOCATION 216240" names the page's first word.
!
! FIFTY-SIX LINES, ALL OF THEM CODE.  Every row emits bits: no DRZ,
! no reservation, and the only non-instruction is line 23's XW.  The
! card-serial column runs EB000300 (line 1) to EB000355 (line 56) --
! fifty-six consecutive serials for fifty-six lines, ONE CARD PER
! LINE, no semicolon double-statement cards.  Counted off the serial
! column, nothing fell off the top or the bottom of the render.
! (This matters: the survey OCR of this page read only lines 2..42
! and its "32 rows, 216241..216274" is a window, not the page.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN IS READ, BUT THE BACKWARD JOIN IS NOT CHECKED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE PAGE PRINTS NO SLC. <<<  216240.40 is printed twice -- as
! line 1's own LOCATION and, as the word, in the header's "LOCATION
! 216240" field -- so the origin below is a READING.  What it is NOT
! is a test of contiguity with printed p.127: pp.121-127 are not
! transcribed, so there is no landed deck to join to, and a hard SLC
! asserts its value rather than checking it (docs/transcription_
! workflow.md, "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE WITH THE ARRIVING
! COUNTER").  The volume survey OCR'd printed p.127's last readable
! row at 216226.00 on ITS line 42, with fourteen more lines below
! that it did not read, so the gap to 216240.40 is consistent with a
! full page but is NOT measured here.  When p.127 lands, compare by
! hand.
!
! THE FORWARD JOIN, by contrast, has two witnesses that agree.  The
! counter leaves line 56 at 216305.40 (line 56 is a half word at
! 216305.00).  The survey OCR of printed p.129 (PDF p.136) reads its
! line 2 at 216306.40 and does not read its line 1 -- a full word at
! 216305.40 puts line 2 at exactly 216306.40.  And line 56 of THIS
! page, "BZXCZ,$+1.32", branches to 216306.40, which is that same
! second instruction of p.129.  Nothing fell off the bottom.
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin here and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G block that printed
! p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed.  Every name this page
! DEFINES is K-prefixed and none collides with anything in pp.2-98.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Three entry points of the interrupt supervisor, laid end to end.
!
! Lines 1-10   the tail of a routine that begins on an earlier page.
!              Line 1 branches to K Q IN (215762.00) on result-zero;
!              otherwise line 2 turns off EOP in the copied control
!              word, and lines 5-10 restore $MR from S T LR, reload
!              the clock and return control with "BE,$".
! Lines 3-4    K SUPP and K SUP CS, two NOPs USED AS BRANCH SLOTS.
!              Each is a "NOP,target" that other rows overwrite:
!              line 12 is "CM1111(BU,1),K SUPP.19" and lines 39/52
!              hit K SUP CS at .19 and .32.  Bit 19 of a half word is
!              the branch-enable bit, so the CM connectives are
!              turning these two NOPs into branches and back.  THAT
!              IS THE PAGE'S CENTRAL IDIOM and it recurs at lines 21,
!              38 and 53.
! Lines 11-22  K COMM R, the communication-region entry: index the
!              channel/unit tables through JCNAD and S CHAN S, store
!              the indicators into S T LR+8.9, reset the K CONCP
!              branch and hand off to P CON E2.
! Line 23      K COMCW, an all-zero index word -- "-CONCEPTOR
!              INTERRUPTS".  It is the page's one data row and the
!              one place the location counter SKIPS: line 22 leaves
!              the counter at 216256.40 and an XW must be full-word
!              aligned, so 216256.40..216257.00 is padding the page
!              does not print.  strap_asm aligns it the same way --
!              line 23's !CHECK at 216257.00 is what demonstrates it.
! Lines 24-35  the CONCEPTOR path: form the CST/UST addresses from
!              S UNIT N, S CHAN N, S UN A and S FI AAC, read the
!              owner's priority level into S M, and branch to K NORM
!              for a PP interrupt or bump the level first for an MCP
!              interrupt.
! Lines 36-41  K CS IN, the channel-signal stacker: convert the
!              channel number in $14 to a bit address, set that bit
!              in the 64-bit queue K CS REG (216312.00), open the
!              K SUP CS switch gate, and spin at K ST CS ("B,$").
! Lines 42-56  K MT CSQ, which empties that queue: C0011 the 64-bit
!              K CS REG into the accumulator, find the first channel
!              with $LZC, compute its status-table address, and test
!              it.  Line 54's CT0001 clears the bit just serviced and
!              line 55 loops; line 56, K Z CS, asks whether any other
!              channel signal is still queued.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE NINE NAMES THIS PAGE DEFINES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Six of them have an INDEPENDENT WITNESS in the volume OCR -- a
! reference printed on a page nobody here has opened, at the address
! this page gives them.  That is a second reading of the spelling,
! which no !CHECK can supply:
!   K SUPP   216242.00  many, e.g. "216034.00  216242.34 C0
!                       BZRZ,KSUPP  -LET IT HAPPEN" and
!                       "216144.00  216242.01 01  LVI,$0,KSUPP"
!   K COMM R 216246.40  vol.2 OCR "216246.65 D0  SVA,MXUAT,KCOMMR"
!   K CONCP  216250.00  vol.2 OCR "216250.23 80 ... ,KCONCP.19"
!   K COMCW  216257.00  vol.2 OCR "216257.00 80 ... ST(BU),KCOMCW
!                       MUST BE CONCEPTORS"
!   K CS IN  216267.00  "221307.00  216267.10 00  B,K CS IN
!                       -STACK CHANNEL SIGNAL"
!   K ST CS  216272.40  "215727.00  216272.40 80  SIC,K ST CS"
! THE THREE WITH NO OFF-PAGE WITNESS are K SUP CS, K MT CSQ and
! K Z CS.  Each is still referenced from a SECOND row on this page
! and compiles bit-exactly at every use (K SUP CS from lines 39 and
! 52, K MT CSQ from lines 4 and 55, K Z CS from line 51), so the
! LOCATIONS are safe; only the SPELLINGS rest on ink alone.
! "MT" in K MT CSQ is settled by line 4's own English: "-BRANCH IF
! CS QUEUE NOT EMTY", i.e. eMpTy.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "CONCEPTOR" IS A REAL MCP ROUTINE, NOT A MISREADING
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 13 and 23 comment "- IF CONCEPTOR,EOP" and "-CONCEPTOR
! INTERRUPTS", which does not look like English.  It is IBM's own
! term: C22-6728 MCP System Analysis Guide prints twelve instances,
! including its table of contents line "F 027  EE  THE CONCEPTOR ,
! PAGE 0135" and a chart headed "CONCEPTOR-CHART 1".  So K CONCP is
! CONCePtor and the comment column is right.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  WHAT IS READ AND WHAT IS CONVENTION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> EVERY ADDRESS BELOW IS BACK-DERIVED FROM A PRINTED
! INSTRUCTION, AND A BACK-DERIVED ADDRESS IS PINNED ONLY TO THE HALF
! WORD. <<<  The printed ".oo" field holds bits 18-23, of which only
! bit 18 is address (the half-word select); bit offsets 0-31 all
! encode identically.  Writing ".0" is a CONVENTION and no !CHECK on
! this page can test it (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "WHAT THE
! ORACLE CANNOT SEE", item 1).  Nine of the nineteen are also landed
! in other decks at the same value, which is a real second reading;
! those are marked LANDED.
!
! SCCW    4.0        LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p102.strap line 282
!                    ("S CCW SYN(BU,64),4.0 -COPIED CONTROL WORD").
!                    Line 2 prints "S CCW+.22" as 000004.26 -- 22
!                    decimal bits = .26 octal -- which checks the
!                    WORD and the offset arithmetic together.
SCCW    SYN(BU,64), 4.0
! SCOMRG  215001.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap line 8
!                    ("S COM RG XW,(8)520000.").  Carried only so
!                    that S M below can be written the way p.103
!                    writes it.
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)215001.0
! SM      215001.05  LANDED, p.103 line 15 "S M SYN(BU,1),
!                    S COM RG+0.05 -LEVEL OF INTERRUPT".  THIS ONE
!                    IS FULLY OBSERVED: line 32 is a VFL store, so
!                    the printed "215001.05" is a BIT address, and
!                    bit 5 is read, not conventional.
SM      SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+0.05
! SCHANS  215002.00  LANDED, p.103 line 30 "S CHAN S SYN,S XCHAN"
!                    with S XCHAN at 215002.00.  Lines 17, 27 and 49
!                    all print 215002.24 B0.  THE PAGE SPELLS IT TWO
!                    WAYS -- "SCHANS" on line 17 and "S CHAN S" on
!                    lines 27 and 49 -- and both compile identically,
!                    which is STRAP ignoring blanks in a name.
SCHANS  SYN, (8)215002.0
! JCNAD   215006.00  >>> NEW HERE, AND IT IS A SECOND NAME FOR A
!                    WORD ALREADY TRANSCRIBED. <<<  Lines 14 and 15
!                    print 215006.34 30 and 215006.24 30, and
!                    decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap puts S YCOCH at
!                    215006.00 (line 37, "S YCOCH VF,(8)23.40",
!                    whose own comment is "-CONSOLE CHANNEL NUMBER").
!                    The volume-2 OCR settles that they are the same
!                    cell.  THE DECISIVE ROW IS "215006.34 30
!                    LV,$14,JCNAD" (docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_250-445.txt
!                    line 3038), which matches line 14 here half word
!                    for half word.  Five more rows there reference
!                    JCNAD at word 215006 with other registers --
!                    ".06" twice, commented "-CONSOLE CHANNEL
!                    ADDRESS" and "-GET CONSOLE CHANNEL NUMBER", and
!                    ".20" twice more -- so the word is JCNAD's and
!                    the English names the same thing S YCOCH's
!                    comment does.  tests/check_symbol_spellings
!                    .py groups them and does NOT flag them, because
!                    JCNAD/SYCOCH is not a drum confusion; it is two
!                    deliberate names, like p.99's S UN A / S UN A A.
JCNAD   SYN, (8)215006.0
! SPROGS  215021.00  LANDED at this value by the p109, p117 and p118
!                    decks.  Line 30 prints 215021.23 01.
SPROGS  SYN, (8)215021.0
! STLR    215230.00  LANDED by p117 and p118; printed p.117 line 12
!                    is the defining card ("S T LR DRZ(BU,64),29").
!                    THREE OFFSETS, ONE BASE, all on this page:
!                    line 9's "S TLR" prints 215230.00, line 8's
!                    "STLR+1.0" prints 215231.44 and line 20's
!                    "STLR+8.9" prints 215240.11 (8 words + 9 decimal
!                    bits = .11 octal).  Spelled with and without
!                    blanks on the same page, as S CHAN S is.
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0
! STIC    215265.00  LANDED by p110, p111, p112 and p118.  Named in
!                    C22-6728's prose -- "the saved IC is stored in
!                    STIC" -- which is what settles the final letter
!                    as C and not O.  Line 5 prints 215265.00 30.
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0
! KQIN    215762.00  NEW.  Line 1 prints 215762.34 C0.  The volume
!                    OCR carries its DEFINING card -- "215762.00
!                    215021.23 01   K Q IN  LVI,9,S PROG S" -- and
!                    two more references, "216170.40  215762.10 C0
!                    B,K Q IN" and "216721.40  215762.10 C0".
!                    >>> THE THIRD GLYPH IS Q, NOT G OR C. <<<
!                    tesseract reads it G, which is worthless here;
!                    what settles it is this page's own ink: line
!                    41's name "K MT CSQ" prints a Q with the same
!                    bowl broken by a diagonal stroke at the lower
!                    right, and line 4's comment "CS QUEUE" prints a
!                    third.  A G on this drum has a bar on the RIGHT
!                    at mid-height; this glyph has none.
KQIN    SYN, (8)215762.0
! KNORM   215776.00  NEW here, but the volume OCR carries its
!                    defining card at "215776.00  000036.37 02
!                    K NORM  LCI,15,30" and about eight references,
!                    every one of which prints 215776.03/.10/.34 --
!                    all bit-18-clear, so the word is even and the
!                    half word is 0.  Lines 33 and 35 here.
KNORM   SYN, (8)215776.0
! KCSREG  216312.00  NEW.  Lines 38, 41 and 54 print 216312.00.  The
!                    volume OCR carries the defining card on a later
!                    page: "216312.00 *  ...  K CS REG DRZ(BU,64),1"
!                    -- a one-word reservation, which is exactly what
!                    a 64-bit channel-signal queue must be.
KCSREG  SYN, (8)216312.0
! PCONE2  216644.00  NEW.  Line 22 prints 216644.10 00.  TWO
!                    INDEPENDENT ROWS IN THE VOLUME OCR give the
!                    NAME at that address: a card at 216644 whose
!                    NAME column reads "P CON E2", and a reference
!                    "216631.40  216644.37 01  LVI,$15,PCONE2".
!                    Only the name and the location are taken from
!                    the OCR; that card's STATEMENT text is too
!                    mangled there to quote and is not relied on.
PCONE2  SYN, (8)216644.0
! The remaining six are VFL FIELD DEFINITIONS, not addresses.  Each
! is copied VERBATIM from the landed deck that defines it, because
! the SYN's mode and length are part of what the referencing rows
! compile -- and because a field symbol's value IS fully observable
! here: it lands in the address field as a bit address.
! SUNAA/SUNA  0.0   LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p99.strap lines
!                   19-20.  p.99 defines S UN A as a second name for
!                   S UN A A on purpose; this page uses "SUNA" on
!                   line 18 and "S UN A" on line 28.
SUNAA   SYN(BU,25), 0.0
SUNA    SYN, SUNAA
! SUNITN  0.47  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p101.strap line 6.
!               OBSERVED: bit 47 is in the SECOND half word, so line
!               24 prints bit 18 SET -- "000000.66", where .26 would
!               be the same register 11 with bit 18 clear.  Compare
!               line 18's "000000.26 3A" for SUNA at 0.0.  That one
!               glyph is a direct reading of the field's offset.
SUNITN  SYN(BU,3), 0.47
! SCHANN  0.12  LANDED, p.101 line 5.  Line 25 prints 000000.24 3C.
SCHANN  SYN(BU,7), 0.12
! SFIAAC  3.0   LANDED, p.101 line 13.  Line 29 prints 000003.32 3C
!               -- the WORD 3 is read off the page.
SFIAAC  SYN(BU,18), 3.0
! SOWNER  0.32  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p99.strap line 30.  Line
!               31 prints 000000.40 8B, and 0o40 = 32 decimal: the
!               bit offset is read, not conventional.
SOWNER  SYN(BU,1), 0.32
! SCHOP   0.26  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p99.strap line 22.  Line
!               51 prints 000000.32 8A, and 0o32 = 26 decimal.  Read.
SCHOP   SYN(BU,1), 0.26
!
! tests/check_symbol_spellings.py was run with this deck alongside
! the repository's: 1046 symbol definitions, NO symbol spelled two
! ways.  It groups this deck's STIC with pp.110/111/112/116/117/118,
! STLR with pp.116/117/118, SPROGS with pp.109/117/118, SM with
! p.103, SCCW with p.102, SUNITN/SCHANN/SFIAAC with p.101, and
! SOWNER/SCHOP/SUNAA with p.99 -- all at the same addresses.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ONE BYTE THAT WAS READ WRONG, AND HOW IT WAS CAUGHT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 28's byte is B-A, not 8-A.  At 900 dpi it reads "8A": this
! drum has worn the TOP-LEFT off the B's vertical stem, which is the
! exact failure docs/transcription_workflow.md names ("B vs 8 differ
! mainly in one vertical stroke, which is the first thing a worn
! drum printer loses").  Re-cropped at 1200 dpi and upscaled, the
! straight left stem and the two right-hand bowls are unmistakable.
! Two further arguments point the same way and were checked BEFORE
! the glyph was re-read, not after: every other V+ on this page
! prints B0 (lines 16, 26, 48) or B0 with an index (line 17, 27, 49),
! and the low nibble A is index $10, exactly as line 18's 3A is
! LV's 30 with the same index.  The correction is recorded here
! rather than silently applied.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS RECORDED AND NOT EXPLAINED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A BARE "*" AFTER THE LOCATION on lines 6, 23 and 40 -- "216243.40 *",
! "216257.00 *", "216272.40 *".  The survey's independent OCR of the
! LOCATION column marks the same three rows, so the marks are on the
! page and not in the render.  printed pp.3, 37, 103 and 120 carry the
! same mark and it was left unexplained on each.  It is NOT a DRZ
! marker (there is no DRZ here) and it is NOT a "$-relative operand"
! marker either: lines 10 ("BE,$") and 56 ("BZXCZ,$+1.32") use $ and
! print no star, while line 23's XW does.  It changes no compiled bit
! and nothing here depends on it.
!
! LINE 11's OPERAND IS "0.0" AND THE CHECK DOES TEST IT.  The page
! prints it as two round glyphs in a STATEMENT operand, where the
! octal-field calibration gives no help.  Measured rather than
! assumed: strap_asm REJECTS "LVI,12,0.O" and "LVI,12,O.O" with
! "undefined symbol 'O'", so the only spelling that assembles at all
! is the one written, and line 11's !CHECK is not passing by the
! assembler's leniency.
!
! THE IBM TYPOS ARE TRANSCRIBED AS PRINTED.  Line 4's comment reads
! "-BRANCH IF CS QUEUE NOT EMTY" and line 21's reads "-RESET RRANCH".
! Both are the listing's own.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! COVERAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ALL FIFTY-SIX ROWS CARRY A !CHECK and all nine symbols a !SYM.
! There is no row on this page that legitimately escapes checking:
! every one emits bits, including line 23's XW, whose printed form
! "000000.00+ 000 000000 000000" is a full index word of zeros.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

        SLC, (8)216240.40

        BZRZ,KQIN                    ! line  1
        CM0000(BU,1),SCCW+.22($13)   ! line  2  -IF NOT, TURN OFF EOP IN CCW
KSUPP   NOP,KCOMMR                   ! line  3
KSUPCS  NOP,KMTCSQ                   ! line  4  -BRANCH IF CS QUEUE NOT EMTY
        LV,0,STIC                    ! line  5
        SV,0,$+2.32                  ! line  6
        LCI,15,29                    ! line  7
        LFT(U),STLR+1.0              ! line  8  -RESTORE $MR
        T,15,STLR,3.0                ! line  9
        BE,$                         ! line 10  -RETURN CONTROL
KCOMMR  LVI,12,0.0                   ! line 11
        CM1111(BU,1),KSUPP.19        ! line 12
KCONCP  B,KCOMCW+1.0                 ! line 13  - IF CONCEPTOR,EOP
        LV,$14,JCNAD                 ! line 14  - CA
        LV,$10,JCNAD                 ! line 15
        V+,$10,$10                   ! line 16
        V+,$10,SCHANS                ! line 17  -CST
        LV,$11,SUNA($10)             ! line 18  -UST
        L(BU,4),KCOMCW.19,1          ! line 19
        ST(BU,5),STLR+8.9            ! line 20  -INDICATORS
        CM0000(BU,1),KCONCP.19       ! line 21  -RESET RRANCH
        B,PCONE2                     ! line 22
KCOMCW  XW,                          ! line 23  -CONCEPTOR INTERRUPTS
        LV,11,SUNITN($12)            ! line 24
        LV,10,SCHANN($12)            ! line 25
        V+,10,$10                    ! line 26
        V+,10,SCHANS                 ! line 27
        V+,11,SUNA($10)              ! line 28
        LV,13,SFIAAC($12)            ! line 29  -OBTAIN ACTIVATED FILE AREA ADD
        LVI,9,SPROGS                 ! line 30
        C0011(BU,1),SOWNER($11),-19  ! line 31  -LEVEL OF INTERRUPT
        ST(BU,1),SM,-19              ! line 32
        BRZ,KNORM                    ! line 33  -BRANCH IF PP INTERRUPT
        V+I,9,1.0                    ! line 34  -MCP INTERRUPT
        B,KNORM                      ! line 35
KCSIN   L(BU,19),$14,-24             ! line 36  -CONVERT CHAN NO TO BIT ADDR
        LV,15,$L                     ! line 37
        CM1111(BU,1),KCSREG($15)     ! line 38  -STACK CHAN SIGNAL
        CM0000(BU,1),KSUPCS.19       ! line 39  -SWITCH GATE OPEN
KSTCS   B,$                          ! line 40
KMTCSQ  C0011(BU,64),KCSREG,64       ! line 41
        LV,11,$LZC                   ! line 42
        LC,14,$AOC                   ! line 43
        Z,$R                         ! line 44
        LF(BU,7),$LZC,45             ! line 45  -FIND CHAN NO
        LV,10,$R                     ! line 46
        LV,14,$10                    ! line 47
        V+,10,$10                    ! line 48
        V+,10,SCHANS                 ! line 49  -COMPUTE CHAN STATUS T ADDR
        SX,14,0                      ! line 50
        BZB,SCHOP($10),KZCS          ! line 51  -CHECK IF CHAN BUSY
        BXCZ,KSUPCS.32               ! line 52  -IF SO, SEE IF ANY OTHER CS IN Q
        CM0000(BU,1),$L($11)         ! line 53
        CT0001(BU,64),KCSREG,64      ! line 54
        B,KMTCSQ+1.0                 ! line 55  -IF SO, LOOP
KZCS    BZXCZ,$+1.32                 ! line 56  -TEST IF ANY OTHER CS IN QUEUE

